s":"cool"},{"text":"நடை","lemma":"நடை","gloss":"agricultural village/tract"}],"gloss":"cool agricultural tracts"},{"surface":"ஒழிய","parts":[{"text":"ஒழி","lemma":"ஒழி","gloss":"to leave behind/renounce"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"leaving behind"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இலம்பாடு","parts":[{"text":"இலம்","lemma":"இலம்","gloss":"poverty"},{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"பாடு","gloss":"suffering/state"}],"gloss":"impoverished"},{"surface":"ஒக்கல்","parts":[{"text":"ஒக்கல்","lemma":"ஒக்கல்","gloss":"kinsmen/relatives"}],"gloss":"kinsmen"},{"surface":"தலைவற்கு","parts":[{"text":"தலைவன்","lemma":"தலைவன்","gloss":"leader/chief"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"கு","gloss":"dative suffix"}],"gloss":"to the leader"},{"surface":"ஓர்","parts":[{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ஓர்","gloss":"one"}],"gloss":"a single"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கரம்பை","parts":[{"text":"கரம்பை","lemma":"கரம்பை","gloss":"wasteland/dry gravel land"}],"gloss":"dry gravel"},{"surface":"சீறூர்","parts":[{"text":"சீறூர்","lemma":"சீறூர்","gloss":"small village"}],"gloss":"small village","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நல்கினன்","parts":[{"text":"நல்கு","lemma":"நல்கு","gloss":"to grant/bestow"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"அன்","gloss":"third person masculine singular suffix"}],"gloss":"he granted"},{"surface":"எனவே","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"என","gloss":"thus"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"thus indeed"}]}],"literal":"O people of the battle camp! O people of the battle camp! / The drummer has a spear in his hand; / the bard with the sweet-stringed small lute made of curved dark horn / has a shield in his hand, appearing beautiful. / Like a densely woven bundle ... / Wearing a withered garland on his head, / with his noble retinue performing the king's duty, / he came to the tall mansion, where discharged arrows swarmed / on his strong, desirable shoulders ... / To the great lord whose blood turned to mud, / as the enemy's long spear pierced through his chest and heart, / he reached the ground with his fat-smeared hero's anklets. / Seeing that, as all those who spread around praised him, / the chief bowed his head and paid homage. / Leaving behind the cool agricultural tracts with swaying ears of grain, / to the leader of his impoverished kinsmen, / he granted a small village of dry gravel land.","translation":"O dwellers of the battle camp, O dwellers of the battle camp!\nThe drummer now holds a deadly spear,\nand the bard, who once played the sweet-stringed small lute\nfashioned from curved dark horn, now holds a shield, looking splendid.\nLike a tightly bound bundle...\nWearing a withered garland on his head,\naccompanied by his noble chiefs performing the king's duty,\nhe entered the tall mansion where a swarm of arrows fell\nupon his mighty, desirable shoulders...\nTo that great warrior whose blood flowed like mud,\nas the enemy's long spear pierced straight through his chest and heart,\nhe fell to the earth, his hero's anklets smeared with fat.\nBeholding this, while all the gathered warriors sang his praise,\nthe great chief bowed his head in deep reverence.\nRenouncing the fertile, cool fields where rich ears of grain sway,\nhe bestowed a small, dry gravel village\nupon the leader of his impoverished kinsmen.","modern":"பாசறையில் உள்ளவர்களே! பாசறையில் உள்ளவர்களே! துடி கொட்டுபவன் கையில் வேல் உள்ளது. வளைந்த கொம்பினால் செய்யப்பட்ட, இனிமையான நரம்புகளைக் கொண்ட சிறிய யாழை வாசிக்கும் பாணனின் கையில் கேடயம் உள்ளது. வாடிய மாலையைத் தலையில் அணிந்த தலைவன், அரசனின் கடமையைச் செய்யும் தன் அரிய சுற்றத்தாரோடு பெரிய மாளிகைக்கு வந்தான். அங்கே பகைவர்கள் எய்த அம்புகள் அவன் மீது மொய்த்தன. அவனது வலிய தோள்களில் அம்புகள் பாய்ந்தன. சேறாக மாறிய குருதியைக் கொண்ட அந்தத் தலைவனுடைய மார்பிலும் நெஞ்சிலும் பகைவரின் நீண்ட வேல் ஊடுருவிச் சென்றது. அதனால், கொழுப்புப் பூசிய வீரக் கழலை அணிந்த கால்களோடு அவன் நிலத்தில் விழுந்து மடிந்தான். அதனைக் கண்டு, சுற்றிலும் பரவி நின்ற வீரர்கள் அனைவரும் புகழும்படி, தலைவணங்கி அவனுக்கு மரியாதை செலுத்தினான் அவனது தலைவன். அத்தலைவன், நெற்கதிர்கள் அசைந்து ஆடும் வயல்கள் சூழ்ந்த குளிர்ந்த மருத நில ஊர்களைப் பிறருக்குக் கொடுத்துவிட்டு, வறுமையில் வாடும் தன் சுற்றத்தாரின் தலைவனுக்குக் கல்லும் முள்ளும் நிறைந்த கரம்பை நிலத்தைக் கொண்ட சிறிய ஊரைக் கொடையாக அளித்தான்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Vākai tiṇai (victory and valour) and the theme of Cālpu Mullai, which extols the noble qualities and selflessness of a warrior and his chief. The poet, Aricil Kiḻār, addresses the warriors in the battle camp, describing the tragic yet glorious death of a brave commander. The commander's retinue, including the drum-beater and the bard, have taken up arms, showing that in times of intense battle, even the artists become warriors. The commander dies heroically on the battlefield, his chest pierced by a long spear, falling to the earth with his fat-smeared hero's anklets. Seeing his supreme sacrifice, the king or chief bows in deep reverence to his fallen soldier. To honor the family of this brave warrior, the chief generously grants a fertile agricultural village to the leader of his impoverished kinsmen, while keeping only the dry, gravelly wasteland for himself, showcasing the ultimate virtue of classical Tamil heroism.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.36],[0.36,0.6],[0.9,1.34],[1.34,1.73],[1.73,2.5],[2.5,3.0],[3.0,3.3],[3.34,3.7],[3.7,4.25],[4.25,4.8],[4.8,5.7],[5.7,6.04],[6.04,7.0],[7.0,7.5],[7.5,7.74],[7.98,8.29],[8.29,8.67],[8.67,9.8],[9.8,10.4],[10.4,10.8],[10.8,11.5],[11.5,12.0],[12.0,13.1],[13.15,13.4],[13.4,13.9],[13.9,14.4],[14.4,15.6],[15.6,15.8],[15.8,16.1],[16.36,17.0],[17.64,18.14],[18.14,18.54],[19.02,19.54],[19.54,19.9],[19.9,20.15],[20.34,20.5],[20.58,21.08],[21.08,21.59],[21.59,22.34],[22.34,22.87],[23.41,24.09],[24.14,24.44],[24.54,24.84],[24.84,25.44],[25.44,25.64],[25.64,26.54],[26.54,26.96],[27.04,27.44],[27.44,28.07],[28.07,28.74],[28.74,29.07],[29.07,29.74],[29.74,30.14],[30.14,30.64],[30.64,31.14],[